---
title: Fyntrac event processing — replica topology and where parallelism comes from
---
flowchart TB
    C["ExcelTestDriver / UI<br/>POST :8081/api/dataloader/model/execute"]
    C --> SVC{{"Service dataloader — type LoadBalancer<br/>round-robins NEW CONNECTIONS, nothing else"}}

    subgraph DLDEP["Deployment dataloader — replicas: 2"]
        direction LR
        DLA["pod A<br/><b>owns this whole run</b><br/>paging · event gen · dispatch<br/>Spring Batch LTD jobs · EOD"]
        DLB["pod B<br/>idle for this run<br/>serves other requests"]
    end

    SVC == "this request pins here<br/>for the entire workflow" ==> DLA
    SVC -. "a different user's request" .-> DLB

    DLA --> T1[["topic fyntrac-python-model-execution<br/>one message per batch of instrumentIds"]]
    DLA -. "at most FYNTRAC_BATCH_MAX_CONCURRENT_DISPATCH = 8<br/>batches in flight (code default 4, k8s sets 8)" .-> T1

    subgraph PYDEP["Deployment dsl-model — replicas: 4 · cpu limit 4 · MAX_PROCESS_WORKERS 4"]
        direction LR
        P1["pod 1<br/>1 batch at a time<br/>4 worker processes"]
        P2["pod 2<br/>1 batch at a time<br/>4 worker processes"]
        P3["pod 3<br/>1 batch at a time<br/>4 worker processes"]
        P4["pod 4<br/>1 batch at a time<br/>4 worker processes"]
    end

    T1 == "ConsumerType.Shared<br/>receiver_queue_size = 1 — no prefetch,<br/>so a batch only goes to a pod that is free" ==> PYDEP

    PYDEP --> DBW[("MongoDB<br/>EventHistory status · TransactionActivity<br/>ModelExecutionBatchLog")]
    PYDEP --> T2[["topic fyntrac-python-model-completion"]]

    T2 == "SubscriptionType.Failover<br/>exactly ONE of the 2 pods is the active consumer" ==> DLB
    DLB --> MC[("Memcached<br/>batch-completion:{correlationId} · TTL 900s")]
    MC == "pod A polls every 250 ms<br/>until its own correlationId appears" ==> DLA

    DLA --> T3[["topic fyntrac-book-gl-staging"]]
    T3 == "Shared" ==> GLP["Deployment gl — replicas: 1<br/>GeneralLedgerEnteryStage<br/>GeneralLedgerAccountBalanceStage"]

    NOTE["<b>Where the parallelism actually is</b><br/>· 2 dataloader replicas parallelize <i>separate</i> requests, never one run<br/>· one run's concurrency = 8 in-flight batches → 4 executing + 4 queued at the broker<br/>· real CPU fan-out = 4 pods × 4 processes = 16 cores of model execution<br/>· LTD aggregation + GL publish run back on pod A, under an in-process ReentrantLock"]

